    "topic": "<code>iam:PermissionsBoundary</code> condition key",
    "stem": "<p>A company wants to enhance its security by applying IAM permissions boundaries. The company tries to use IAM policy conditions and receives the following error:</p>\n<p>\"Error: error updating IAM Role (role-name) assume role policy: AccessDenied: User: id-arn is not authorized to perform: iam:UpdateAssumeRolePolicy on resource: role role-name status code: 403, request id: request-id\"</p>\n<p>The policy that contains the condition includes the following snippet:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n    &quot;Version&quot;: &quot;2012-10-17&quot;,\n    &quot;Statement&quot;: [\n        {\n            &quot;Sid&quot;: &quot;CreateOrChangeOnlyWithBoundary&quot;,\n            &quot;Effect&quot;: &quot;Allow&quot;,\n            &quot;Action&quot;: &quot;UpdateAssumeRolePolicy&quot;,\n            &quot;Resource&quot;: &quot;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/role-name&quot;,\n            &quot;Condition&quot;: {\n                &quot;StringEquals&quot;: {\n                    &quot;iam:PermissionsBoundary&quot;: &quot;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:policy/MyBoundaryPolicy&quot;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>What is the reason for the error?</p>",
